                                                                  8431 1451
  General methodology: The global approach considered in this     8431 1451
          work is presented in the following paper: Modern        8431 1451
          nuclear data evaluation with the TALYS code system,     8431 1451
          A.J. Koning and D. Rochman, Nuclear Data Sheets 113     8431 1451
          (2012) 2841.                                            8431 1451
                                                                  8431 1451
  MF2:  Resolved resonance range  (RRR)                           8431 1451
       The RRR was generated with TARES-1.31, compiled on         8431 1451
       12-10-2015 11:58:11 PM at Villingen  , Switzerland. The RRR8431 1451
       expands from 0 to 5.709901E+3 eV. A total of               8431 1451
       2 l-values are used and 22 resonances. The resonance       8431 1451
       formalism is multi-level Breit Wigner (MLBW).              8431 1451
       The ladder approach from the CALENDF code is used to       8431 1451
       generate statistical resonances in the unresolved          8431 1451
       resonance range. Therefore, the URR is translated into     8431 1451
       resolved resonance range. Explanations about the method    8431 1451
       can be found in the CALENDF manual: CEA-Report CEA-R-6277  8431 1451
       "CALENDF-2010: User manual" by J.C. Sublet, P. Ribon and   8431 1451
       M. Coste-Delcaux.                                          8431 1451
       The method of creating statistical resonances in the       8431 1451
       URR region is described in: "From average parameters to    8431 1451
       statistical resolved resonances", D. Rochman et al.,       8431 1451
       Annals of Nucl. Ene. 51 (2013) 60.                         8431 1451
       The s-wave average level spacing is 558 eV and             8431 1451
       the s-wave neutron strength is 6.748e-05 1e-4.             8431 1451
                                                                  8431 1451
       After the ladder method, the retroactive method is applied 8431 1451
       to update the MF32 and MF2 with the SAMMY code.            8431 1451
                                                                  8431 1451
  MF32: Covariance file for resonance parameters                  8431 1451
        The compact format is used to represent the covariance    8431 1451
        information on the resonance parameters. Uncertainties    8431 1451
        come from compilations, EXFOR or existing libraries and   8431 1451
        correlations between parameters are obtained following    8431 1451
        the method presented in NIM/A 589 (2008) 85.              8431 1451
        SAMMY is used in the retroactive mode to update MF32.     8431 1451
                                                                  8431 1451
